Nerve disorders and pain referred to the shoulder (@shoulder-referred: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @shoulder, #source @med-source-msd-shoulder, #source @med-source-upper-limb-nerves, #source @med-source-plexus, #medicine @shoulder-systemic, #orthopedics @shoulder-systemic, #shoulder @shoulder-systemic) { r_7BFZ7QKTEBQWTCQD9A60VXWDH5
**Read:** the neck and shoulder relationships in [Avaliação do ombro — Manual MSD](../../../sources/Avaliacao-do-ombro-MSD.lingua#r_51H0EB6JRBDW2X2HNEBY52FG6X), then [Upper-limb nerves — NCBI Bookshelf](../../../sources/Upper-limb-nerves.lingua#r_6G2RDX948Y8KGMDFRV226X4RH6) and [Brachial plexus — NCBI Bookshelf](../../../sources/Brachial-plexus.lingua#r_5RBF38QWEQ2D9CXZAN1ERZ4F8X) for the anatomy.

Pain experienced at the shoulder can arise from the shoulder region or be referred from elsewhere, including cervical structures. A spinal-root disorder and a peripheral nerve disorder occupy different points in the network. Altered sensation, strength, reflexes, and other findings help distinguish possibilities; a distribution drawn in an atlas is an approximation.

Suprascapular, axillary, long thoracic, and accessory nerve disorders can affect different muscle functions. Scapular prominence or weakness has a differential diagnosis rather than a single automatic explanation. Significant new neurological change warrants clinical assessment.

Shoulder or arm pain associated with chest discomfort, breathlessness, or other systemic symptoms changes the urgency of the question. Do not assume an orthopedic cause because pain is felt near a joint.

**Try:** trace a hypothetical signal interruption at a root and at a named nerve. Compare their possible territories, then state why anatomy alone cannot identify the cause of an individual's symptoms.

